Wi-Fi to the robot isn't allowed at events: tether over USB-A, or an adapter into the radio.␀␀␀%.2f : 1␀␀␀␀%.0f rpm␀␀␀␀%.2f m/s Â· %.1f ft/s at the wheel␀␀%.1f NÂ·m␀␀␀%.0f N (%.0f lbf) of push at stall␀␀no current limit: the stall figures apply␀␀␀%.1f rev/s Â· %.0f Â°/s at the output␀␀␀%.0f lbfÂ·in at the output, at stall␀␀␀␀%d Ã— %.0f A = %.0f A drawn at stall␀␀␀␀at %d A stator per motor Â· %.0f N of push␀␀at %d A stator per motor (%.0f %% of stall)␀motors on the shaft␀reduction␀␀␀â€“␀+␀␀␀wheel␀␀␀stator current limit, amps␀␀free speed␀␀stall torque␀␀␀␀torque at the limit␀Ideal: no losses. Real mechanisms reach roughly 80â€“90 % of these.␀Wire for its breaker (the usual FRC table; check this season's manual):
â€” 40 A breaker: 12 AWG or thicker
â€” 30 A: 14 AWG Â· 20 A: 18 AWG Â· 5 A and under: 22 AWG
â€” battery to main breaker to power hub: 6 AWG, 120 A main breaker
Red, white, brown or yellow for +12 V; black or blue for ground.
Tug-test every crimp and Wago. A connection that is warm after a match is failing.␀␀␀Two 120 Î© terminators, one at each end of the chain.
Power off, meter CAN-H to CAN-L: about 60 Î© is healthy; about 120 Î© means one terminator is missing; near 40 Î© means one too many; open means a break.
Yellow is CAN-H, green is CAN-L.
Devices dropping out together: look where the chain passes them (connector, pinched wire), not at the devices. Keep bus load well under 80 %.␀␀Resting (off the charger for an hour, robot off):
â€” 12.8-13.0 V: full Â· about 12.4 V: charge it before a match
Under load the voltage sags; the controller browns out near 6.8 V and cuts the motors first.
Internal resistance (a battery analyser) is the real test: under about 0.015 Î© is match-ready; a battery that climbs past about 0.02 Î© is for practice.
Check the lugs are tight and the heat-shrink is whole: a loose lug looks like a bad battery.␀␀␀Before blaming code: spin it by hand (binding), check the breaker, check it is on the CAN chain and its firmware is current.
A brushless motor turning the wrong way is inverted in code, never by swapping wires.
Supply limit: protects the breaker and battery. Stator limit: caps torque and heat.
Hot after a match (too hot to hold): stalled or over-geared â€” check the gearing app.␀␀␀wiring␀␀can bus␀60␀␀80␀␀2 in␀␀␀␀3 in␀␀␀␀4 in␀␀␀␀6 in␀␀␀␀3:1␀5:1␀6.75 (L2)␀␀␀8.14 (L1)␀␀␀12:1␀␀␀␀25:1␀␀␀␀50:1␀␀␀␀100:1␀␀␀X60␀X60 foc␀X44␀X44 foc␀Falcon␀␀Falcon foc␀␀Minion␀␀NEO␀Vortex␀␀NEO 550␀zero here␀␀␀î␀against the robot␀␀␀encoder says␀␀␀␀encoder minus gravity␀␀␀level zeroed here␀␀␀level zero cleared␀␀saved Â· %.0f s in lens/␀␀␀␀clip on its way to the pc␀␀␀couldn't send the clip␀␀recording Â· %d of %d s␀sc2356 Â· 2 mp␀␀the camera didn't start␀the camera isn't running␀␀␀␀îŒ␀%s/lens␀%04d%02d%02d-%02d%02d%02d.h264␀␀%s/%s␀␀␀the encoder didn't start␀␀␀␀%s/%04d%02d%02d-%02d%02d%02d.jpg␀␀␀␀%d this session Â· %s/lens␀␀couldn't save␀␀␀bus load␀␀␀␀/s␀␀reading %sâ€¦␀␀␀%s Â· %u records Â· %d:%02d

